// Sleepy
// Sleepy — Cozmo rework (2026-07-11, docs/assets/cozmo.jpg "Sleepy Eyes"):
// FLAT half-closed lid, no bevels (slopes of -0.5 left a residual "line"
// under the eyes — PLAYBOOK-HW §4e).
// OffsetY: PINNED TO THE BOTTOM OF THE EYE ZONE (user 08-03), which SUPERSEDES
// the verdict of 2026-07-12 recorded here — that one asked for the lower edge to
// sit where a NORMAL eye has it (70/2 = 35 below centre), and that is what -19
// gave. It is written down rather than overwritten: a preset value with a user's
// name on it is not a free parameter, and the next reader has to be able to see
// that the earlier answer was replaced on purpose and not lost.
//
// The zone is 160 px tall and centred at EYE_CY = 80, so its floor is +80 from
// centre. The eyes rest TWENTY pixels above it, at +60 (user 08-03) — low
// enough to read as "sinking", not so low that they merge with the status band.
// Nothing can push them off that line either: the Brain freezes every VERTICAL
// channel for Sleepy (gaze y, breathing, squashY) while leaving the horizontal
// ones alone, so the rest is genuinely still and the eyes can still glance
// sideways. 60 - 32/2 = 44; the sign is flipped by EyeRig::mirrored, so a
// NEGATIVE preset value means downward. The lid still drops onto a bottom that
// does not move — the A2.17 falling-lid invariant is untouched, only the line
// it falls to has.
static const sce::EyeConfig Preset_Sleepy = {
    /* OffsetX                        */ 0,
    /* OffsetY                        */ -44,
    /* Height                         */ 32,
    /* Width                          */ 100,
    /* Slope_Top                      */ 0.00f,
    /* Slope_Bottom                   */ 0.00f,
    /* Radius_Top                     */ 12,
    /* Radius_Bottom                  */ 6,
    /* Inverse_Radius_Top             */ 0,
    /* Inverse_Radius_Bottom          */ 0,
    /* Inverse_Offset_Top             */ 0,
    /* Inverse_Offset_Bottom          */ 0
};

